//anatomy.canonical.com/StyleKey> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/key.appearance.background> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/tokenNamespace> \"surface.color.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/key.appearance.background> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/tokenNamespace> \"modifier.color.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/key.appearance.background> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/tokenNamespace> \"color.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/key.appearance.background> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/valueKind> \"either\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/key.appearance.background> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"appearance.background\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/key.appearance.background> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/StyleKey> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/projectionField> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"documentationStages\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/projectionField> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"summary\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/projectionField> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"_meta.title\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/projectionField> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Dot-delimited GraphQL field path relative to the enclosing data context. On a node: the field the node renders. On a relation: the traversal populating the slot. Names the field only, never an unwrapping path like edges/node — whether a plural field is a connection or a plain list is a provider mechanism discovered from the schema. The relation's cardinality maps onto the field's shape: upper bound to multiplicity, lower bound to nullability.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/projectionField> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/projectionField> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/Projection> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/projectionField> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"projection field\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/projectionField> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/propValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"spinner\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/propValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"checkmark\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/propValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"chevron-down\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/propValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"The fixed value the anatomy pins the prop to.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/propValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/propValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/Prop> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/propValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"prop value\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/propValue> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/propName> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"icon\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/propName> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Name of the pinned prop, as defined on the referenced component in the design system ontology.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/propName> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/propName> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/Prop> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/propName> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"prop name\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/propName> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/projectionType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"Pattern\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/projectionType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"OntologyClass\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/projectionType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"Component\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/projectionType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"GraphQL type condition, like a Relay fragment's 'on'. On a root node it establishes the data context for the tree; on a child it narrows the traversed entity's type, like an inline fragment.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/projectionType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/projectionType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/Projection> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/projectionType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"projection type\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/projectionType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/styleState> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"invalid\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/styleState> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"indeterminate\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/styleState> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"expanded\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/styleState> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"selected\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/styleState> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"disabled\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/styleState> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"focus\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/styleState> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"active\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/styleState> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"hover\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/styleState> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Interaction state this style value applies in. Absent\\n    means the default state. Closed vocabulary (hover, active, focus,\\n    disabled, selected, expanded, indeterminate, invalid), governed by\\n    registry — 'active' subsumes Material's 'pressed' and Spectrum's 'down';\\n    'focus' maps to CSS :focus-visible (Spectrum's 'key-focus'); 'expanded'\\n    is a disclosure's open state ([open], aria-expanded); 'indeterminate' is\\n    a mixed checkbox or progress bar; 'invalid' is a failed validation\\n    (:invalid, aria-invalid). States re-value style channels only: they never\\n    add structure (that is the Switch construct) and never define transitions\\n    or interaction logic (state machines stay out of scope). Authored as an\\n    @state suffix on the style key.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/styleState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/styleState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"style state\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/styleState> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/styleValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"[modifier.color.icon, modifier.color.text, currentColor]\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/styleValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"[modifier.color.text, color.text]\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/styleValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"dimension.100\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/styleValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"flow\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/styleValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"The AUTHORED SPELLING of the value, verbatim: a scalar\\n    as written, a sequence in its flow form. It is the evidence of what the\\n    reference says, and it is kept even where anatomy:consumes carries the\\n    same symbols in a form a query can walk — the terminal literal of a\\n    fallback chain lives only here, because a literal is not a symbol.\\n\\n    A value is a symbol, a primitive, or a sequence whose elements are\\n    symbols with at most one primitive and only as the last element. The\\n    slash-delimited path and the trailing '?' marker are RETIRED: an element\\n    that resolves nowhere is a register row and a comment, not a sigil.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/styleValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/styleValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/Style> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/styleValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"style value\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/styleValue> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/styleKey> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"typography.weight\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/styleKey> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"appearance.background\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/styleKey> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"spacing.internal.inline.start\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/styleKey> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"layout.type\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/styleKey> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Platform-agnostic style property identifier.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/styleKey> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/styleKey> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"style key\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/styleKey> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/slotName> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"icon\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/slotName> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"footer\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/slotName> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"header\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/slotName> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"default\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/slotName> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Named slot in the parent that this child maps to.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/slotName> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/slotName> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/Relation> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/slotName> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"slot name\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/slotName> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/cardinality> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"2..5\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/cardinality> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"1..*\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/cardinality> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"0..*\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/cardinality> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"0..1\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/cardinality> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"1\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/cardinality> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Instance count constraint on the child.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/cardinality> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/cardinality> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/Relation> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/cardinality> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"cardinality\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/cardinality> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/discriminator> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"override\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/discriminator> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"internal\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/discriminator> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"props\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/discriminator> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"What determines which case applies.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/discriminator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/discriminator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/Switch> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/discriminator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"discriminator\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/discriminator> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/role> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"icon container\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/role> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"spacer element\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/role> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"content wrapper\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/role> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Human-readable purpose of an anonymous node.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/role> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/role> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/AnonymousNode> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/role> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"role\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/role> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/uri> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"global.subcomponent.card_header\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/uri> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"global.subcomponent.accordion-item\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/uri> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"global.component.button\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/uri> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Unique identifier for a named node within the design system.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/uri> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/uri> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/NamedNode> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/uri> <https://pragma.canonical.com/graphql#name> \"anatomyUri\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/uri> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"uri\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/uri> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/consumes> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"( dt:modifier.color.text dt:color.text )\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/consumes> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"The token symbols this style binding consumes, as an\\n    ordered rdf:List whose elements are dt:TokenSymbol individuals in FALLBACK\\n    ORDER: rdf:first is the primary symbol, and each rest is what the\\n    implementation falls back to when the one before it is undefined. It is\\n    the RDF form of the authored value — a one-to-one transcription of the\\n    implementation's `var(a, var(b, …))` chain — and the reason the list and\\n    not a single symbol is that the fallback is a per-slot choice: a\\n    component's background and its text fall back differently, so no rule\\n    declared once on a symbol can carry it.\\n\\n    A slot consumes a CHANNEL by name where the implementation reads the\\n    channel (`modifier.color.text`) and the semantic token by name where it\\n    reads the token; nothing is inferred from the spelling. A terminal\\n    literal the chain ends in (`currentColor`, `0`, `1em`) is NOT an element\\n    here — it resolves against nothing by design — and is carried in\\n    anatomy:styleValue, which keeps the authored spelling verbatim as\\n    evidence. Whether a key carries this at all is anatomy:valueKind's\\n    business, and whether a symbol RESOLVES is the consumer's: a name no\\n    stratum declares is kept as consumed with a register row.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/consumes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#List> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/consumes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/Style> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/consumes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"consumes\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/consumes> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/hasProp> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Attaches a pinned prop value to a named node. Named nodes only: anonymous nodes have no prop surface to pin.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/hasProp> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/Prop> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/hasProp> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/NamedNode> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/hasProp> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"has prop\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/hasProp> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/hasProjection> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Attaches a graph-data projection to a node or relation.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/hasProjection> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/Projection> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/hasProjection> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> _:fc90e440a261fa84ec5b65d5b62f4640 .\n_:b3c6a7d1145944002c32a4ce26163b7a <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .\n_:cc15b966b2f09aba9f6e1556501e6a64 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:b3c6a7d1145944002c32a4ce26163b7a .\n_:b3c6a7d1145944002c32a4ce26163b7a <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/Relation> .\n_:fc90e440a261fa84ec5b65d5b62f4640 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#unionOf> _:cc15b966b2f09aba9f6e1556501e6a64 .\n_:cc15b966b2f09aba9f6e1556501e6a64 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/Node> .\n_:fc90e440a261fa84ec5b65d5b62f4640 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/hasProjection> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"has projection\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/hasProjection> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/hasStyle> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Attaches a style declaration to a node.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/hasStyle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/Style> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/hasStyle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/Node> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/hasStyle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"has style\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/hasStyle> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/caseNode> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Node this case resolves to.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/caseNode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/Node> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/caseNode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/SwitchCase> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/caseNode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"case node\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/caseNode> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/hasCase> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"An alternative within this switch.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/hasCase> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/SwitchCase> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/hasCase> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/Switch> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/hasCase> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"has case\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/hasCase> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/edgeSwitch> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Polymorphic switch this edge connects to.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/edgeSwitch> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/Switch> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/edgeSwitch> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/Edge> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/edgeSwitch> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"edge switch\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/edgeSwitch> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/edgeTarget> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Child node this edge connects to.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/edgeTarget> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/Node> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/edgeTarget> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/Edge> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/edgeTarget> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"edge target\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/edgeTarget> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/hasRelation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Relation qualifying this edge.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/hasRelation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/Relation> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/hasRelation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/Edge> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/hasRelation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"has relation\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/hasRelation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/hasEdge> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Connects a node to a child relationship.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/hasEdge> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/Edge> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/hasEdge> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/Node> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/hasEdge> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"has edge\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/hasEdge> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/rootNode> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Top-level node of an anatomy specification.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/rootNode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/NamedNode> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/rootNode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/Specification> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/rootNode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"root node\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/rootNode> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/tokenNamespace> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"spacing.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/tokenNamespace> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"modifier.color.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/tokenNamespace> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"color.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/tokenNamespace> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"A dotted prefix, ending in a dot, whose symbols the key\\n    admits — matched against a symbol's dotted NAME with STRSTARTS, never\\n    against its IRI. Multi-valued, and a key whose base namespace is `N.`\\n    carries `N.`, `modifier.N.` and `surface.N.`: a channel of a symbol in\\n    `N.` is exactly what the anatomy consumes where the implementation reads\\n    the channel, so without the channel spellings every channel binding in\\n    the corpus would be a namespace violation. It is the single declaration of\\n    which symbols a key admits, and the inverse question — which keys admit\\n    this symbol — is the query over it (dt:appliesTo is retired).\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/tokenNamespace> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/tokenNamespace> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/StyleKey> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/tokenNamespace> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"token namespace\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/tokenNamespace> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/valueKind> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"either\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/valueKind> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"primitive\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/valueKind> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"token\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/valueKind> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"What the key admits: \\\"token\\\" (a symbol, or a list of\\n    symbols ending at most in one primitive), \\\"primitive\\\" (a literal the\\n    implementation writes as it stands), or \\\"either\\\". Measured from the\\n    reference declarations mapped onto the key when the roster was taken —\\n    all reading a var() is token, none is primitive, mixed is either. An\\n    \\\"either\\\" key compiles to an sh:or in StyleShape: it carries\\n    anatomy:consumes, or it carries a primitive styleValue.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/valueKind> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/valueKind> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/StyleKey> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/valueKind> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"value kind\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/valueKind> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/StyleKey> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"typography.color\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/StyleKey> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"spacing.internal.inline.start\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/StyleKey> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"appearance.background\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/StyleKey> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"One canonical style key: a platform-agnostic property\\n    the anatomy may bind. The roster was measured, not designed: it is the\\n    right-hand column of a table whose left-hand column was every CSS property\\n    the reference implementations bind, so a key exists because an\\n    implementation binds the property, never because the vocabulary looked\\n    incomplete. registry.ttl states where that measurement lives.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/StyleKey> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Style Key\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/StyleKey> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/SwitchCase> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"One alternative within a Switch.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/SwitchCase> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Switch Case\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/SwitchCase> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/Switch> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Polymorphic position admitting several alternatives.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/Switch> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Switch\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/Switch> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/Prop> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"A pinned property value: the anatomy fixes one prop of\\n    the referenced component at this tree position (e.g. the icon component's\\n    'icon' prop pinned to 'chevron-down' for an intrinsic chevron). References\\n    a property defined in the design system ontology — the DSL never defines\\n    the prop surface itself. Whether the pinned prop exists on the component,\\n    and whether the value is admissible, is validated by consumers holding\\n    the design system graph.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/Prop> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Prop\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/Prop> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/Projection> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Fragment-style binding to graph data, after the Relay\\n    colocation pattern. On a node it declares a type condition (like a\\n    fragment's 'on') and/or the field the node renders; on a relation it\\n    declares the traversal that populates the slot.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/Projection> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Projection\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/Projection> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/Style> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"A single style declaration binding a property key to a value.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/Style> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Style\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/Style> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/Relation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Metadata qualifying a parent-child relationship.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/Relation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Relation\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/Relation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/Edge> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Reified parent-child relationship in the anatomy tree.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/Edge> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Edge\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/Edge> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/AnonymousNode> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Structural element without design system identity.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/AnonymousNode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Anonymous Node\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/AnonymousNode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/Node> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/AnonymousNode> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/NamedNode> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Design system entity instantiable by consumers.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/NamedNode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Named Node\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/NamedNode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://anatomy.canonical.com/Node> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/NamedNode> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/Node> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Position in the anatomy tree.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/Node> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Node\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/Node> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/Specification> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Root of an anatomy file.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/Specification> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Specification\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/Specification> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Meta-model for the Anatomy DSL — a YAML-based language\\n    for describing design system component structure.\\n\\n    Models anatomy files as trees of nodes connected by reified edges.\\n    Inspired by the Relay GraphQL connection pattern.\\n\\n    Consolidates WD404 (core), WD404.1 (addendum 1), projections\\n    (addendum 2): fragment-style bindings of nodes and relations to\\n    graph data, prop pinning (addendum 3): fixed prop values on\\n    referenced components, and interaction states (addendum 4):\\n    state-scoped style values.\\n\\n    OUT OF SCOPE (matching the DSL itself):\\n    - Prop surface definition — names, types, and optionality of a\\n      component's props live in the design system ontology. Pinned prop\\n      VALUES are in scope as of addendum 3.\\n    - State MACHINES — transitions, triggers, and interaction logic.\\n      Appearance PER interaction state is in scope as of addendum 4\\n      (styleState); structural state variation remains the Switch\\n      construct's job.\\n    - Modifier descriptions (only token references)\\n\\n    Validation shapes defined in shapes.ttl.\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> \"Compliant with OWL DL profile\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Anatomy DSL Ontology\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> \"0.4.0\" .\n<https://anatomy.canonical.com/> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/rank> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Must be a positive integer no greater than the length of the tuple's anatomy:consumes list.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/rank> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"The symbol's 1-based position in the style tuple's fallback order; 1 is the primary. A value's terminal primitive is not a symbol and carries no record, so ranks count symbols only.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/rank> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"rank\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/rank> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/rank> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/TokenBinding> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/rank> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/node> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"A role alone would collide: global.pattern.table_of_contents binds role 'link' at three depths with identical styles.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/node> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"The node's TREE PATH in the viaBlock's tree, not its role: \\\"$root\\\", then one step per edge descended, joined by \\\"/\\\". A node edge's step is the child's uri, or its role where it has no uri; a switch edge's step is case[<name>]; a step whose name recurs among its siblings carries a 1-based ordinal in brackets.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/node> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"node\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/node> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/node> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/TokenBinding> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/node> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/viaBlock> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Part of the record's identity, not an attribute: a block's own root binding and one inherited from a subcomponent's root share node, key, state and rank.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/viaBlock> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"The tree the binding was reached through: the record's own block for an own-tree binding, the referenced block for an inherited one. Equal to the subject in the own-tree case, so an inherited binding is FILTER(?viaBlock != ?block) with no special case.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/viaBlock> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"viaBlock\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/viaBlock> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://ds.canonical.com/UIBlock> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/viaBlock> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/TokenBinding> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/viaBlock> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/consumesSymbol> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Must name a symbol declared in S1 or minted into S2, unless anatomies/register.yaml admits the element under X1, X2, X5, X7 or X15.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/consumesSymbol> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"The dt:TokenSymbol this record consumes: the rank-th member of the style tuple's anatomy:consumes list. Exactly one per record, and determined by the record's six-tuple identity.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/consumesSymbol> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"consumesSymbol\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/consumesSymbol> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://dt.canonical.com/TokenSymbol> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/consumesSymbol> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/TokenBinding> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/consumesSymbol> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/consumesSymbol> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasTokenBinding> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Derived; one record per identity tuple, so a subcomponent referenced twice yields one record and not two.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasTokenBinding> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"A token binding of this block: one record per consumed symbol per rank, over the block's own anatomy tree and the trees of every block its anatomy references.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasTokenBinding> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"hasTokenBinding\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasTokenBinding> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://ds.canonical.com/TokenBinding> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasTokenBinding> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/UIBlock> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/hasTokenBinding> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/TokenBinding> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Derived by deriveTokenBindings from the block's ds:anatomyDsl literal and the transitive closure of its uri: references. Never hand-asserted.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/TokenBinding> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"One symbol a UIBlock consumes, at one node of one tree, for one style key, in one interaction state, at one rank of the fallback order. A record is a blank node in the block's own per-instance file; its identity is the six-tuple (block, viaBlock, node, styleKey, styleState, rank) and ds:consumesSymbol is functionally determined by it.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/TokenBinding> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Token Binding\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/TokenBinding> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/libraryTier> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Must reference a valid ds:Tier instance\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/libraryTier> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"The design system tier that this library implements\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/libraryTier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"libraryTier\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/libraryTier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://ds.canonical.com/Tier> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/libraryTier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/ImplementationLibrary> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/libraryTier> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/documentation> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Must be a valid URL\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/documentation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Documentation link if different from main artifact\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/documentation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"documentation\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/documentation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/documentation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/ImplementationLibrary> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/documentation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/link> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Must be a valid URL\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/link> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"URL to the library's main artifact or repository\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/link> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"link\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/link> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/link> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/ImplementationLibrary> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/link> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/platform> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Should be a recognised platform name\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/platform> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"The platform or technology this library targets (e.g. React, Web Components, Flutter)\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/platform> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"platform\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/platform> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/platform> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/ImplementationLibrary> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/platform> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/libraryName> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Must match the published package identifier\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/libraryName> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"The package or library name as published (e.g. npm package name)\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/libraryName> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"libraryName\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/libraryName> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/libraryName> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/ImplementationLibrary> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/libraryName> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/isDraft> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Must be true or false\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/isDraft> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Whether this implementation is in draft state and not yet ready for production use\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/isDraft> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"isDraft\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/isDraft> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/isDraft> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/ImplementationObject> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/isDraft> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/importStatement> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Must be a complete import statement naming the published package specifier and an export the package really provides. ABSENT rather than guessed when the implementation is not reachable by name from the library's entry point — a subcomponent published only as a property of its parent (Breadcrumbs.Item) or an internal file carries none.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/importStatement> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"The statement a consumer pastes to bring this implementation into a file, naming the published package (e.g. 'import { Button } from \\\"@canonical/react-ds-global\\\";'). Derived from the name the library's public entry point actually exports the implementation's source file under, not from the file name.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/importStatement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"importStatement\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/importStatement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/importStatement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/ImplementationObject> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/importStatement> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/importStatement> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/versionedLink> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Must be a valid URL including version tag\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/versionedLink> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"URL to a specific tagged version of this implementation in source control\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/versionedLink> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"versionedLink\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/versionedLink> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/versionedLink> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/ImplementationObject> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/versionedLink> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/headLink> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Must be a valid URL\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/headLink> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"URL to the latest/HEAD version of this implementation in source control\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/headLink> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"headLink\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/headLink> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/headLink> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/ImplementationObject> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/headLink> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/library> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Must reference a valid ds:ImplementationLibrary instance\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/library> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"The implementation library that contains this implementation\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/library> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"library\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/library> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://ds.canonical.com/ImplementationLibrary> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/library> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/ImplementationObject> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/library> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/library> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/implementationVersion> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Should follow semver format\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/implementationVersion> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Version of this specific implementation, independent of the UIBlock version\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/implementationVersion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"implementationVersion\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/implementationVersion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/implementationVersion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/ImplementationObject> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/implementationVersion> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/implementationVersion> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/implementsBlock> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Must reference a valid ds:UIBlock instance\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/implementsBlock> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"The UIBlock that this implementation realises in code\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/implementsBlock> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"implementsBlock\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/implementsBlock> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://ds.canonical.com/UIBlock> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/implementsBlock> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/ImplementationObject> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/implementsBlock> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/implementsBlock> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/constraints> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Should describe the valid value space for this property. Format varies by property type.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/constraints> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Constraints on valid values for this property. For choice types, lists allowed values (e.g. '[primary, secondary, tertiary]'). For numbers, specifies ranges. For objects, describes required structure.\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/constraints> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"constraints\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/constraints> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/constraints> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/Property> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/constraints> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/defaultValue> <https://ds.canonical.com/acceptanceCriteria> \"Must be a valid value for the property's type\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/defaultValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"The default value for this property when not explicitly set by the consumer\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/defaultValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"defaultValue\" .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/defaultValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/defaultValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ds.canonical.com/Property> .\n<https://ds.canonical.com/defaultValue> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypePro